   668	        # file_write to an EXISTING file if there has been no successful
   669	        # file_read of it since the path's last successful mutation in this
   670	        # conversation. A NEW (nonexistent) file is always allowed — there is no
   671	        # prior content to ground on. The old F3 "second untracked write forces
   672	        # replace" escape hatch is REMOVED; the only way past this refusal is an
   673	        # actual file_read (which sets the read-since-write bit), or using a
   674	        # targeted edit tool (file_replace_lines / file_insert_lines / file_edit)
   675	        # which does not require a full-rewrite guard because it operates on
   676	        # specific lines anchored to the current content.
