     1	"""W2 — file-state tracker for the workspace snapshot (per-path SHA-based staleness).
     2	
     3	Extracted as a standalone module (no loop-state dependency) so it can be
     4	tested independently of the engine. The tracker is a mutable object held
     5	by ``ViewBuilder`` across turns; it is NOT reconstructed from the event log
     6	(SHA comparison is the ground truth, not event-sourced replication).
     7	
     8	Responsibilities:
     9	  * Track the SHA of each file the snapshot has shown in full (so the next
    10	    turn can compare disk-sha to known-sha and decide: full vs. pointer).
    11	  * ``record_agent_io`` — call after a successful file_read or file_write /
    12	    file_edit / file_append; pre-registers the new SHA so a self-write is
    13	    never falsely flagged as an external change.
    14	  * ``stale_paths`` — async scan: for each known path, read from disk and
    15	    return paths whose disk-SHA diverges from the last-seen SHA.
    16	  * ``file_state_notice`` — module-level pure function: empty stale list →
    17	    None (silent, the common fast-path); else a named "re-read these" block.
